- zsh traps: brace every variable next to a `:` (`${N}:…`), quote `====` separators, **no `cd`** (scripts may `cd` inside themselves by `${0:A:h}`), every path absolute and single-quoted (they contain `!`). macOS has no `timeout`: bound the local starts with a background process and `kill` after 120 s. `measure402.zsh` needs its execute bit (B316 slip 8).

